    <div class="content" id="contentArea">
      <!-- ===== CARDS ===== -->
      <div id="graphical-intro" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">1</span><h2>Graphical Representation — आलेखीय प्रस्तुति</h2></div><p><strong>Graphical Representation</strong> data को <strong>visual form</strong> (charts, graphs, diagrams) में present करना है।</p><div class="formula-box">Graph = Visual Data Presentation + Easy Interpretation + Quick Comparison</div><p><strong>Advantages:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Easy to understand and interpret</li><li>Quick comparison of values</li><li>Shows trends and patterns clearly</li><li>Attractive and engaging</li><li>Simplifies complex data</li></ul><p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>May be misleading if not properly constructed</li><li>Approximate values (not precise)</li><li>Requires basic chart-reading skills</li></ul></div>

      <div id="bar-chart" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">2</span><h2>Bar Chart — दण्ड आरेख</h2></div><p><strong>Bar Chart</strong> rectangular bars (rectangles) का उपयोग करता है — bar की <strong>height</strong> या <strong>length</strong> value को दर्शाता है।</p><div class="formula-box">Bar Chart = Categories + Rectangular Bars + Height/Length = Value</div><p><strong>Key Characteristics:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Bars have <strong>equal width</strong></li><li>Bars are <strong>separated by gaps</strong></li><li>Used for <strong>discrete/categorical data</strong></li><li>Bars can be <strong>vertical or horizontal</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Types of Bar Charts:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li><strong>Simple Bar Chart:</strong> Single bar per category</li><li><strong>Multiple/Grouped Bar Chart:</strong> Multiple bars per category</li><li><strong>Stacked/Component Bar Chart:</strong> Bars divided into components</li><li><strong>Percentage Bar Chart:</strong> Stacked bars showing percentages</li><li><strong>Deviation Bar Chart:</strong> Bars above/below a baseline</li></ul><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Department-wise enrollment</li><li>State-wise literacy rate</li><li>Year-wise sales comparison</li><li>Male-Female distribution</li></ul></div>

      <div id="histogram" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">3</span><h2>Histogram — आयतचित्र</h2></div><p><strong>Histogram</strong> <strong>continuous frequency distribution</strong> को दिखाने के लिए उपयोग किया जाता है।</p><div class="formula-box">Histogram = Continuous Data + Adjacent Rectangles + Area = Frequency</div><p><strong>Key Characteristics:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Rectangles are <strong>adjacent</strong> (no gaps between bars)</li><li>Used for <strong>continuous data</strong></li><li>X-axis shows <strong>class intervals</strong></li><li><strong>Area</strong> of rectangle represents frequency</li><li>Used for <strong>frequency distribution</strong> display</li></ul><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Marks distribution of students</li><li>Age distribution of population</li><li>Height/Weight distribution</li><li>Any grouped frequency data</li></ul><p><strong>Unequal Class Intervals:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>When class widths are unequal, use <strong>Frequency Density</strong></li></ul><div class="formula-box">Frequency Density = Frequency / Class Width</div></div>

      <div id="bar-vs-histogram" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">4</span><h2>Bar Chart vs Histogram — दण्ड आरेख vs आयतचित्र</h2></div><table class="data-table"><tr><th>Basis</th><th>Bar Chart</th><th>Histogram</th></tr><tr><td>Data Type</td><td>Discrete/Categorical</td><td>Continuous</td></tr><tr><td>Bars</td><td>Separated by gaps</td><td>Adjacent (no gaps)</td></tr><tr><td>Height</td><td>Represents value</td><td>Represents frequency (or density)</td></tr><tr><td>Area</td><td>Not meaningful</td><td>Represents frequency</td></tr><tr><td>X-axis</td><td>Categories</td><td>Class intervals</td></tr><tr><td>Order</td><td>Can be changed</td><td>Fixed order (class intervals)</td></tr><tr><td>Width</td><td>Equal (usually)</td><td>Follows class interval</td></tr></table></div>

      <div id="pie-chart" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">5</span><h2>Pie Chart — वृत्त आरेख</h2></div><p><strong>Pie Chart</strong> एक circle (pie) को sectors में विभाजित करता है — प्रत्येक sector एक <strong>part of the whole</strong> को दिखाता है।</p><div class="formula-box">Pie Chart = Circle + Sectors + Angle = Percentage Share</div><p><strong>Key Characteristics:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Shows <strong>part-to-whole</strong> relationship</li><li>Total = 100% (or 360°)</li><li>Each sector angle = (Value / Total) × 360°</li><li>Used for <strong>categorical data</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Formulae:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li><strong>Sector Angle:</strong> (Component Value / Total) × 360°</li><li><strong>Percentage Share:</strong> (Component Value / Total) × 100</li></ul><p><strong>Quick Conversions:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>1% = 3.6°, 10% = 36°, 25% = 90°</li><li>50% = 180°, 75% = 270°</li></ul><p><strong>Example:</strong> Total = 800, Science = 200 → 200/800 × 100 = 25% → 25% × 360° = 90°</p><p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Not good for many categories (overcrowding)</li><li>Difficult to compare similar-sized sectors</li></ul></div>

      <div id="line-chart" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">6</span><h2>Line Chart — रेखा आरेख</h2></div><p><strong>Line Chart</strong> data points को <strong>lines</strong> से connect करता है — shows <strong>trends over time</strong>.</p><div class="formula-box">Line Chart = Points + Lines + Time = Trend</div><p><strong>Key Characteristics:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Shows <strong>trends and patterns</strong> over time</li><li>Used for <strong>time-series data</strong></li><li>Multiple lines for comparison</li><li>X-axis usually shows <strong>time</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Interpretation:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Upward slope → Increase</li><li>Downward slope → Decrease</li><li>Horizontal line → No change</li><li>Steeper slope → Faster change</li></ul><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Year-wise GDP growth</li><li>Monthly sales trend</li><li>Annual pass percentage</li><li>Population growth over years</li></ul><p><strong>Exam Trap:</strong> Steepness depends on the scale of axes — truncated or unequal axes may exaggerate change.</p></div>

      <div id="table-chart" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">7</span><h2>Table Chart — सारणी आरेख</h2></div><p><strong>Table Chart</strong> data को <strong>rows और columns</strong> में present करता है — shows <strong>exact numerical values</strong>.</p><div class="formula-box">Table Chart = Rows + Columns + Exact Values</div><p><strong>Key Characteristics:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Shows <strong>precise numbers</strong></li><li>Multiple variables can be shown together</li><li>Easy to calculate ratios, percentages, averages</li><li>Rows and columns with clear headings</li></ul><p><strong>Advantages:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Precise values available</li><li>Comparisons easy</li><li>All data in one place</li></ul><p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p><ul class="bullet-list"><li>Trend less immediately visible than in a line chart</li><li>Can be overwhelming with too much data</li></ul><p><strong>Example:</strong></p><table class="data-table"><tr><th>Course</th><th>2024</th><th>2025</th><th>% Change</th></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>200</td><td>250</td><td>25%</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>300</td><td>360</td><td>20%</td></tr><tr><td>C</td><td>250</td><td>300</td><td>20%</td></tr></table></div>

      <div id="chart-selection" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">8</span><h2>Which Chart to Use? — कौन-सा आरेख उपयोग करें?</h2></div><table class="data-table"><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Best Chart</th></tr><tr><td>Category comparison</td><td>Bar Chart</td></tr><tr><td>Continuous frequency distribution</td><td>Histogram</td></tr><tr><td>Part-to-whole relationship</td><td>Pie Chart / Component Bar</td></tr><tr><td>Time trend</td><td>Line Chart</td></tr><tr><td>Exact numerical values</td><td>Table Chart</td></tr><tr><td>Relationship between two variables</td><td>Scatter Plot</td></tr></table></div>

      <div id="exam-traps" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">9</span><h2>Common Exam Traps — सामान्य परीक्षा जाल</h2></div><ul class="bullet-list"><li><strong>Trap 1:</strong> Bar chart has gaps; histogram does not → ✅ Correct distinction.</li><li><strong>Trap 2:</strong> Histogram is for discrete data → ❌ Histogram is for continuous data.</li><li><strong>Trap 3:</strong> Bar chart = continuous data → ❌ Bar chart is for discrete/categorical data.</li><li><strong>Trap 4:</strong> Pie chart sector angles = percentage × 3.6 → ✅ 1% = 3.6°.</li><li><strong>Trap 5:</strong> Line chart = part-to-whole → ❌ Line chart shows trends; pie chart shows part-to-whole.</li><li><strong>Trap 6:</strong> Table chart = shows trends best → ❌ Table shows exact values; line chart shows trends.</li><li><strong>Trap 7:</strong> In histogram, height of bar = frequency always → ❌ For unequal class intervals, frequency density is used.</li></ul></div>

      <div id="practice-questions" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">10</span><h2>Practice Questions — अभ्यास प्रश्न</h2></div>
      <div class="pyq-tag">Question 1</div>
      <p>Which chart is best for comparing sales of different products?</p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>A. Pie chart</li><li>B. Bar chart</li><li>C. Histogram</li><li>D. Line chart</li></ul>
      <div class="answer-box">Answer: B. Bar chart</div>
      <p class="explain">Explanation: Bar chart is best for comparing categories.</p>

      <div class="pyq-tag">Question 2</div>
      <p>Which chart is used for continuous frequency distribution?</p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>A. Bar chart</li><li>B. Histogram</li><li>C. Pie chart</li><li>D. Line chart</li></ul>
      <div class="answer-box">Answer: B. Histogram</div>
      <p class="explain">Explanation: Histogram is used for continuous frequency distribution.</p>

      <div class="pyq-tag">Question 3</div>
      <p>In a pie chart, a sector represents 20% of the total. What is the sector angle?</p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>A. 20°</li><li>B. 36°</li><li>C. 72°</li><li>D. 90°</li></ul>
      <div class="answer-box">Answer: C. 72°</div>
      <p class="explain">Explanation: Angle = 20% × 360° = 72°.</p>

      <div class="pyq-tag">Question 4</div>
      <p>Which chart is most suitable for showing a trend over years?</p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>A. Bar chart</li><li>B. Pie chart</li><li>C. Line chart</li><li>D. Histogram</li></ul>
      <div class="answer-box">Answer: C. Line chart</div>
      <p class="explain">Explanation: Line chart shows trends over time.</p>

      <div class="pyq-tag">Question 5</div>
      <p>What is the key difference between a bar chart and a histogram?</p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>A. Bar chart has gaps; histogram does not</li><li>B. Histogram has gaps; bar chart does not</li><li>C. Both have gaps</li><li>D. Neither has gaps</li></ul>
      <div class="answer-box">Answer: A. Bar chart has gaps; histogram does not</div>
      <p class="explain">Explanation: Bar chart bars are separated by gaps; histogram bars are adjacent (no gaps).</p>

      <div class="pyq-tag">Question 6</div>
      <p>Total marks = 500. A student scored 150 marks in Science. What is the central angle in a pie chart?</p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>A. 72°</li><li>B. 90°</li><li>C. 108°</li><li>D. 120°</li></ul>
      <div class="answer-box">Answer: C. 108°</div>
      <p class="explain">Explanation: (150/500) × 360° = 0.3 × 360° = 108°.</p></div>

      <div id="one-page-revision" class="topic-card"><div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">11</span><h2>One-Page Revision — एक पेज में पुनरावृत्ति</h2></div>
      <div class="formula-box">Bar Chart = Categories + Gaps | Histogram = Continuous + No Gaps</div>
      <div class="formula-box">Pie Chart = Part-to-Whole | Line Chart = Trend | Table = Exact Values</div>

      <p><strong>Bar Chart:</strong></p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>Discrete data, gaps between bars, height = value</li>
      <li>Types: Simple, Multiple, Stacked, Percentage</li></ul>

      <p><strong>Histogram:</strong></p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>Continuous data, no gaps, area = frequency</li>
      <li>Frequency Density = f / Class Width (for unequal intervals)</li></ul>

      <p><strong>Pie Chart:</strong></p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>Part-to-whole, Angle = (Value/Total) × 360°</li>
      <li>1% = 3.6°, 25% = 90°, 50% = 180°</li></ul>

      <p><strong>Line Chart:</strong></p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>Time trends, points connected by lines</li>
      <li>Up = Increase, Down = Decrease, Flat = No change</li></ul>

      <p><strong>Table Chart:</strong></p>
      <ul class="bullet-list"><li>Rows + Columns + Exact values</li>
      <li>Good for precise calculations</li></ul>

      <p><strong>Exam Formula:</strong></p>
      <div class="formula-box">Chart → Data Type → Purpose → Key Feature</div>
      <p><em>UGC NET में Graphical Representation के questions chart identification, interpretation, और calculation पर based होते हैं।</em></p></div>

